import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Validate StateKnot locally."
  description="A contributor tutorial for installing the pinned toolchain and reproducing the repository's executable quality gates."
  section="Getting started"
>
  <aside class="docs-callout" aria-labelledby="tutorial-scope-title">
    <h2 id="tutorial-scope-title">Scope of this tutorial</h2>
    <p>
      This validates the implementation that exists today. The typed Agent
      contract, first-party OpenAI Responses and Anthropic Messages adapters,
      atomic admission, and durable run/result reads are implemented. The
      provider-native end-to-end Agent graph and stable service API have not
      shipped.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="prerequisites-title">
    <h2 id="prerequisites-title">Prerequisites</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Git.</li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://rustup.rs/">rustup</a>; the repository pins Rust 1.88.0
        with the minimal profile, rustfmt, and Clippy.
      </li>
      <li>
        PostgreSQL is optional for the fast workspace gate and required for the
        provider integration suite.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="typed-agent-next-title">
    <h2 id="typed-agent-next-title">Run the typed contract examples</h2>
    <p>
      The next tutorial constructs the real schema-pinned Agent contract and
      both provider adapters without external I/O or credentials. Continue to
      <a href="/docs/typed-agent/">Build a typed Agent contract</a> after the workspace
      gate passes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="checkout-title">
    <h2 id="checkout-title">Clone and run the complete local gate</h2>
    <p>
      Run these commands from a clean checkout. rustup reads
      <code>rust-toolchain.toml</code> automatically.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Shell · repository validation</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="getting-started-commands"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="getting-started-commands"
        tabindex="0"><code>git clone https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot.git
cd StateKnot
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked
RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc --workspace --all-features --no-deps --locked</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="results-title">
    <h2 id="results-title">Read the result correctly</h2>
    <p>A green local gate proves that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the pinned compiler accepts every workspace target and feature;</li>
      <li>
        the core contract, canonical wire, property, and unit tests pass; and
      </li>
      <li>public Rust documentation contains no warnings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      It does not exercise a live PostgreSQL server, a live model-provider
      account, MCP, A2A, or a live durable Agent Loop. CI runs the
      database-backed Runtime and storage-provider suites separately against
      PostgreSQL 16 and 17; model-adapter transport tests use a real local TCP
      server.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="postgres-test-title">
    <h2 id="postgres-test-title">Run the PostgreSQL integration suite</h2>
    <p>
      Point the suite at a disposable database. The test role must be able to
      create and drop a temporary database because startup and migration
      failures are part of the contract.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Shell · disposable PostgreSQL only</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="postgres-test-command"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="postgres-test-command"
        tabindex="0"><code>STATEKNOT_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE \
STATEKNOT_REQUIRE_POSTGRES_TESTS=1 \
cargo test -p stateknot-store-postgres --test postgres --locked -- --test-threads=1</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      Never point this command at a production or shared database. Continue with
      the <a href="/docs/postgresql/">PostgreSQL provider guide</a> for the production-shaped
      connection and migration boundary.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
